			"customizationId": "monk_huian",
			"height": 178,
			"weight": 150,
			"backgroundStory": "Born into a family of village schoolteachers, Chen Shouren entered a monastery after soldiers burned the school where he taught. He first trained with the staff so he would never again be helpless when others needed protection, but years of tending the monastery's elderly brothers softened his anger. Now an accomplished instructor, Hui'an speaks quietly and gives even the most awkward novice his full attention. He takes a particular interest in small sects that shelter displaced people, though he watches how their leaders treat the weakest disciples before offering his trust.",
			"refuseText": "They're doing fine, thank you...",
			"acceptText": "Our disciples could use a patient teacher.",
			"joinText": "Master, I am Hui'an. I've taught martial arts at my monastery for years. I hear you've taken in many people with nowhere to go. I'd like to stay and help look after them.",
