			"backgroundStory": "Xu Yongkang grew up in a farming village and first came to the monastery seeking grain after a failed harvest. He stayed to help in the kitchens, discovered a talent for staff fighting, and eventually took his vows. Pushan now oversees the monastery's meals and stores, remembering which novices need larger portions and which elderly monks struggle with hard food. His broad frame and cheerful manner cause visitors to underestimate his speed. Having once depended on strangers' generosity himself, he is quick to welcome refugees and equally quick to notice when the rice supply is running low.",
